1
00:05:26,666 --> 00:05:32,666
He's not looking for trouble...he's wearing it.

2
00:10:53,333 --> 00:10:59,333
The Tuxedo is a thriller, action, comedy film directed by Kevin Donovan.

3
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Cabbie-turned-chauffeur Jimmy Tong learns there is really only one rule when you work for
playboy millionaire Clark Devlin : Never touch Devlin's prized tuxedo.

4
00:21:46,666 --> 00:21:52,666
But when Devlin is temporarily put out of commission in an explosive accident, Jimmy puts on the tux
and soon discovers that this extraordinary suit may be more black belt than black tie.

5
00:27:13,333 --> 00:27:19,333
Paired with a partner as inexperienced as he is,
Jimmy becomes an unwitting secret agent.

6
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:46,000
Jimmy Tong, played by Jackie Chan.

7
00:38:06,666 --> 00:38:12,666
Del Blaine, played by Jennifer Love Hewitt.

8
00:43:33,333 --> 00:43:39,333
Clark Devlin, played by Jason Isaacs.

9
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:06,000
Steena, played by Debi Mazar.

10
00:54:26,666 --> 00:54:32,666
Dietrich Banning, played by Ritchie Coster.

11
00:59:53,333 --> 00:59:59,333
Dr. Simms, played by Peter Stormare.

12
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:26,000
The Tuxedo is a 2002 American science fiction action comedy film directed by
Kevin Donovan and starring Jackie Chan and Jennifer Love Hewitt.

13
01:10:46,666 --> 01:10:52,666
The spy parody involves a special tuxedo that
grants its wearer superhuman abilities.

14
01:16:13,333 --> 01:16:19,333
The plot surrounds a corporate terrorist who threatens to poison the United States' fresh water supply
with bacteria that spills electrolytes into the blood and totally dehydrates the host.

15
01:21:40,000 --> 01:21:46,000
The film received negative reviews from critics upon release and earned
a total worldwide box office gross of $104.4 million.

16
01:27:06,666 --> 01:27:12,666
The film explores themes of new york city, martial arts, chauffeur, bomb, spy.

17
01:32:33,333 --> 01:32:39,333
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking and intense.
